{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics","id":1339174,"title":"Shield Mechanics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-03T07:38:16-07:00","id":1339174,"title":"Shield Mechanics","content":"I was wondering if anybody has worked/tried changing combat uses for shields in 3rd ed? I am not fan of current system, but don't wont to unbalance things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10745-nosleeves","name":"nosleeves","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T07:48:52-07:00","id":1339178,"title":"","content":"What would you like shields to be able to do that they currently can't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T08:14:21-07:00","id":1339182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nosleeves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics#post1339174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering if anybody has worked/tried changing combat uses for shields in 3rd ed? I am not fan of current system, but don't wont to unbalance things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most shields are Medium weapons, so give +1 Parry. They do less damage than regular weapons (as, I think, a shield bash should) and they let you flurry a Full Defence (such as with a Rush as you use your shield to cover your advance). If it's an Artifact, you can unlock Evocations to improve your Defence.<br /> <br /> That's pretty powerful.<br /> <br /> I can see an argument for giving a bonus to Clashes. And I can see an argument for being usable in either hand without penalty. Maybe Flurry a Full Defence with Aim? But any more than that and you're going to unbalance things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T08:34:06-07:00","id":1339188,"title":"","content":"I would may be kind of like shields to have a larger benefit when paired with medium weapons. Currently the only benefit is you can flurry a Full Defence with a non-attack action, which 90% of the time means Disengage or Rush. This isn't an irrelevant benefit, but it's not that hot: Flurry gives you a -1 Defence penalty anyway, so if you flurry Disengage and Full Defence you're paying 2i and taking -3 on the Disengage roll for +1 Defence, which is a small enough thing that, in my experience, basically no-one ever bothers with a shield.<br /> <br /> On the other hand... for genre reasons, do I really care that PCs and villains just use a one-handed sword two-handed, or use the other one for stunts? Maybe not. I think the only thing is I'd like Battle Groups to benefit from shields (or be penalised by not having them). Admittedly, I often just give Battle Groups shields even though it gives them 0 benefits in every fight I've ever run with them, because I think it fits, and so maybe, again, it doesn't matter that much.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I will say that combining a Shield with a short sword/handaxe/other small weapon is really good already though.<br /> I can see that PCs would like a useful benefit from having a shield, but maybe a short sword/shield combo is enough for that. And I guess Artefact shields give useful defensive (or other) evocations. Though I haven't loved any of the shields in Arms/Lunars/Dragonblood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T08:38:46-07:00","id":1339190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339182#post1339182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most shields are Medium weapons, so give +1 Parry...<br /> <br /> That's pretty powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is.... but longswords, axes, maces, etc, also give +1 Parry and it doesn't stack, so if you're using any of them you don't get the benefit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I can see an argument for being usable in either hand without penalty. Maybe Flurry a Full Defence with Aim? </div> </div> </div>Those seem like decent ideas. Although I'm kind on the fence about it making sense to combine Aim with Full Defence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T09:02:39-07:00","id":1339195,"title":"","content":"I liked the idea of being able to use them as light cover via the &quot;take cover&quot; action, personally, although I haven't had the opportunity to really play it out.<br /> <br /> While it isn't suggested in the rules, I wouldn't say it is denied either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T09:13:51-07:00","id":1339199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339195#post1339195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the idea of being able to use them as light cover via the &quot;take cover&quot; action, personally, although I haven't had the opportunity to really play it out.<br /> <br /> While it isn't suggested in the rules, I wouldn't say it is denied either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have also considered this myself due to the fact that shields seem very lacking otherwise, and it makes sense both mechanically and thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25108-ikeulhu","name":"ikeulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T09:40:49-07:00","id":1339204,"title":"","content":"You might have better balance options by splitting it up. For example a tower shield can be placed to act as heavy cover, an action that can be flurries, but can\u2019t be used to flurry a full defense with anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T12:22:20-07:00","id":1339226,"title":"","content":"It's definitely worth considering houseruling that shield flurries have none of the usual flurry penalties, both for simplicity's and for its functionality's sake. It's also definitely Melee charmspace to allow shields to flurry with attacks, but it seems it'll be touchy to balance since it's sort of a cap buster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T12:28:42-07:00","id":1339227,"title":"","content":"I'd just have them count as light armour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T14:42:35-07:00","id":1339243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339226#post1339226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's definitely worth considering houseruling that shield flurries have none of the usual flurry penalties, both for simplicity's and for its functionality's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit hesitant, but actually that might be fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also definitely Melee charmspace to allow shields to flurry with attacks, but it seems it'll be touchy to balance since it's sort of a cap buster. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... 2i and a -3 attack penalty for +1 Defence isn't so attractive that I'd think it cap-busting tech. (Assuming it's not combined with the above).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd just have them count as light armour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. Like the current rules there's issues around stacking; it's of no benefit for anyone who's wearing light armour anyway.<br /> <br /> Maybe you could count it as light armour, and if they've got light armour and a shield it counts as medium armour. Possibly if they've got medium armour and a shield it counts as heavy armour.<br /> <br /> And for heavy armour and a shield... meh. Guys in full lobster plate often didn't fight with shields anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T15:09:38-07:00","id":1339246,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's the fuller version of the idea, that I've posted elsewhere. <br /> <br /> Heavy armour + shield doesn't help cos it's redundant at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T15:13:02-07:00","id":1339247,"title":"","content":"We've had fairly long thread about the Shield Tag in the past.<br /> <br /> In my mind, it's a badly written tag. The damage penalty is crippling, the ability to Flurry Full Defense is is niche and unsustainable without Charms (though it's not bad for Full Defense + Defend Other too), the Flexible Tag ignores it, it has no benefit for most weapons stat blocks (and is actively bad to attach to some), does nothing for BGs, and it's basically not worth it compared to using your off-hand for either the double weapon Clash bonus or having two different weapons to get access to multiple more valuable Tag/stat block combinations. <br /> <br /> The best solutions I've come up with is splitting it up between two Tags. One for the Full Defense aspect (and possibly a Clash bonus), and one for providing Cover based on the weapon type. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T21:19:10-07:00","id":1339303,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> &quot;Most shields are Medium weapons, so give +1 Parry. They do less damage than regular weapons (as, I think, a shield bash should) and they let you flurry a Full Defence (such as with a Rush as you use your shield to cover your advance). If it's an Artifact, you can unlock Evocations to improve your Defence.&quot;<br /> <br /> A &quot;shield bash&quot; is basically taking a 15 lb iron,wood and rawhide mace and driving it into your face or ribcage. <u>You can kill people with a shield bash</u>. It shouldn't be any less lethal than a spear through the ribs or a sword to the neck.<br /> <br /> &quot;That's pretty powerful.&quot;<br /> <br /> Its.... not.<br /> <br /> The argument over shields is endlessly amusing for me, since it usually devolves into explaining how broken and nonsensical the majority of the other combat mechanics are.<br /> <br /> What I do to &quot;fix&quot; shields, but please keep in mind that my games were 1) geared towards mortal characters, and 2) pretty simulationist, as much as the system would let me<br /> <br /> - shields allow the user to use the &quot;Full Defense&quot; Action in a Flurry, although Flurries can't normally contain attack actions<br /> - They also lend a +2 Bonus to Clash Attacks<br /> - They allow the user to Take Cover as (Dexterity + Dodge) Reflexive Action at reduced Difficulty (0 Difficulty for Light Cover at -1 Initiative Cost, and 1 Difficulty for Heavy Cover at -2 Initiative Cost)<br /> - Shields give the wielders a -1 Mobility Penalty, to represent the weight and heft of the weapon, as well as its tendency to interfere with movement and strikes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","user":"Boston123","date":". 10-04-2019, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T05:20:50-07:00","id":1339338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339190#post1339190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is.... but longswords, axes, maces, etc, also give +1 Parry and it doesn't stack, so if you're using any of them you don't get the benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you don't get a Parry benefit from having a sword in one hand and a mace in the other either... so? I don't follow the complaint.<br /> <br /> Light weapon for the Accuracy bonus. Shield for Parry.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339303#post1339303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A &quot;shield bash&quot; is basically taking a 15 lb iron,wood and rawhide mace and driving it into your face or ribcage. <u>You can kill people with a shield bash</u>. It shouldn't be any less lethal than a spear through the ribs or a sword to the neck.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can kill people with a dagger. You can kill people with a tea cup.<br /> <br /> I'd rather take a shield to the face than a mace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-04-2019, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T05:24:48-07:00","id":1339339,"title":"","content":"Heck, you can kill people by lightly shoving them, if they fall wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T06:00:50-07:00","id":1339343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339243#post1339243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... 2i and a -3 attack penalty for +1 Defence isn't so attractive that I'd think it cap-busting tech. (Assuming it's not combined with the above).</div> </div> </div> </div>The flurry defense penalty is rather easily negated by charms already. I don't recall a scene long penalty negator that cuts it, but it's still cheap.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T06:02:50-07:00","id":1339344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339338#post1339338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you don't get a Parry benefit from having a sword in one hand and a mace in the other either... so? I don't follow the complaint.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The complaint is that if you've got an axe or mace or longsword, in Exalted the benefits of having a shield are so marginal that I've never seen anyone in 3rd ed ever take advantage of them (in fact, off the top of my head, I can't think of any 3rd ed PC I've seen ever carry one, and NPCs only ever used them for stunt fodder).<br /> <br /> Whereas in real life, as almost every historical line infantry force that relied on longswords/axes/one-handed spears paired them with shields, I assume they felt that the shields were giving them some very useful benefit.<br /> <br /> (We both agree that small weapons/shields work fine though. Like Roman legionairres with short swords and huge shields. Well, more than fine, it's a really good combo in Exalted. Might use a shield/short daiklaive for my next character, though I don't know what I'll do with the free second short daiklaive! And all the published ones use evocation trees that are about two-weapon fighting. Hmmm, are there are any other light artefact melee weapons written up...)<br /> <br /> This bothers me less than Boston123, as my games are less simulationist than his. I've been generally happy to have martial artists dueling with straight swords and no shields.<br /> But my current game is basically vikings vs samurai, and your average viking comes with axe and shield. Yet the shield does nothing.<br /> It's not a huge issue for me; I just give them all shields anyway. But it seems a bit silly that it'd be mechanically better to give them a second large axe, which wasn't something vikings did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-04-2019, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T06:06:56-07:00","id":1339345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339343#post1339343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flurry defense penalty is rather easily negated by charms already. I don't recall a scene long penalty negator that cuts it, but it's still cheap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which ones? But if that's the case, yeah, flurrying Full Defence and Attack might be a bit good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T06:28:51-07:00","id":1339350,"title":"","content":"Also, on the subject of shield's damage penalty, it's probably worth noting that in Exalted shields are no worse at breaking people's skulls and splattering their brains everywhere than metal maces, morningstars, warhammers, quarterstaffs, etc.<br /> <br /> What they're bad at (well, the same as your bare hand) is knocking people back, hooking their weapons out the way, pushing them into their friends, helping you drive them back and position yourself better, tripping your opponents up, hitting them in the face and stunning them allowing you to get a good stab in with yourr sword, etc.<br /> In fact, shields are actually the worst weapon in the game for the above. They're only good for actually knocking people out when you've already used your sword to get yourself in the perfect position to strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T06:36:20-07:00","id":1339353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339345#post1339345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which ones? But if that's the case, yeah, flurrying Full Defence and Attack might be a bit good.</div> </div> </div> </div>general negators, basically. Dipping Swallow, Bulwark, Flow Like Blood","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T07:12:29-07:00","id":1339367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339338#post1339338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you don't get a Parry benefit from having a sword in one hand and a mace in the other either... so? I don't follow the complaint.<br /> <br /> Light weapon for the Accuracy bonus. Shield for Parry.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're carrying a weapon in each hand:<br /> <br /> Carrying the same weapon in both hands = +2 dice to Clashes. So if thinking you're using a medium weapon in one hand, there's pretty much no reason not to carry two for this bonus.<br /> <br /> Carrying two different weapons = get the most out of the diversity this allows.<br /> <br /> The complaint is that the Shield Tag isn't rarely better than any other Tag to include in a mixed weapon setup. A whip on one hand for lots of Tags, and a sword or one handed spear in the other for the medium weapon +1 Parry and better ability to deal with high armor value is way more effective than a short sword and a shield; despite one being a kinda ridiculous combo that there isn't even much in the way of inspiration for, and the other is the infantry standard of the inspiration for the settings current most powerful military.<br /> <br /> The complaint is that the Shield Tag sucks so nobody wants to use them even if they have a concept that would use a shield, and thus should be better so shield using characters makes sense; and this should work for mortal characters, not just characters that can use Artifacts and Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can kill people with a dagger. You can kill people with a tea cup. </div> </div> </div>Neither of those take a -2 damage penalty to attack people with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd rather take a shield to the face than a mace. </div> </div> </div>I'd rather be shot with a 9mm pistol than a 12 gauge shotgun... but neither is a &quot;good&quot; option.<br /> <br /> The issue is that shields aren't armor. They're not a passive thing strapped on to you. They're active weapons used to control fights and harm opponents as much as whatever you might pair them with. The damage penalty on them doesn't make sense from a simulation perspective, or the abstraction of the system, or the perspective of doing cool shit like being Exalted Captain America.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T09:00:20-07:00","id":1339384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339344#post1339344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas in real life, as almost every historical line infantry force that relied on longswords/axes/one-handed spears paired them with shields, I assume they felt that the shields were giving them some very useful benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the ability to rapidly advance on an enemy position, protected by the shield so you don't die but somewhat encumbered by the weight?<br /> <br /> Something like being able to Rush without the Defence penalty, but taking -3 to the dice pool?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339367#post1339367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're carrying a weapon in each hand:<br /> <br /> Carrying the same weapon in both hands = +2 dice to Clashes. So if thinking you're using a medium weapon in one hand, there's pretty much no reason not to carry two for this bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I said I'd be okay with giving that same bonus to Shields.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339367#post1339367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The complaint is that the Shield Tag sucks so nobody wants to use them even if they have a concept that would use a shield, and thus should be better so shield using characters makes sense; and this should work for mortal characters, not just characters that can use Artifacts and Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Short sword and Shield.<br /> Javelins and Shield.<br /> Whip and Shield.<br /> <br /> Could you use a sword instead? Sure. But Exalted has lots of suboptimal choices (see Chopping Sword vs Axe).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339367#post1339367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither of those take a -2 damage penalty to attack people with.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Dagger has Damage +7.<br /> A Shield has Damage +7.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339367#post1339367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather be shot with a 9mm pistol than a 12 gauge shotgun... but neither is a &quot;good&quot; option.</div> </div> </div> </div>And eating a Damage +7 attack isn't a &quot;good option&quot;, but it's better than a +9.<br /> <br /> I'd probably model the difference in damage between a 9mm and a 12 gague as a +2 (+9 and +11).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339367#post1339367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is that shields aren't armor. They're not a passive thing strapped on to you. They're active weapons used to control fights and harm opponents as much as whatever you might pair them with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a sword. And they give +1 Parry, like a sword. And they can be used to make attacks, like a sword. But they are less deadly than a sword. And you can argue that shields are just as deadly as swords, but there's a reason historically armies which used shields carried an actual weapon do do their killing with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339367#post1339367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The damage penalty on them doesn't make sense from a simulation perspective,</div> </div> </div> </div>Shields aren't as effective a weapon as swords. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339367#post1339367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or the abstraction of the system,</div> </div> </div> </div>It's harder to kill someone with a slab of blunt wood than a pointy metal object. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339367#post1339367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or the perspective of doing cool shit like being Exalted Captain America.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's literally what Charms, Martial Arts and Evocations are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-04-2019, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T09:53:57-07:00","id":1339395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339384#post1339384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I said I'd be okay with giving that same bonus to Shields.<br /> ...But Exalted has lots of suboptimal choices (see Chopping Sword vs Axe).</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you see to get the core complaint just fine. The Shield Tag isn't good. People want it to not be sub-optimal, instead of just accepting it as sub-optimal and not fixing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Dagger has Damage +7.<br /> A Shield has Damage +7. </div> </div> </div>A medium shield as Damage + 7. A light shield has Damage + 5. A teacup, as an improvised weapons, has Damage + 7, cost 1i per attack, and can be used with Melee or Brawl freely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like a sword. And they give +1 Parry, like a sword. </div> </div> </div>No, this is just a factor of the medium weapon stat blocks, not swords vs. shields. A short sword (light stat block) or a two-handed sword (heavy stat block) don't give you a +1 Parry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But they are less deadly than a sword. </div> </div> </div>Only in the representation of lethal vs. bashing damage. Killing people doesn't care about weapon damage in Exalted 3e. Weapon damage is about Initiative, which shields are tactically better for than swords. You control the fight (aka get more Initiative than your opponent) with your shield, and stab them with the sword for a lethal damage Decisive attack.<br /> <br /> And even that is more genre emulation than reality. In reality blunt force trauma is quite deadly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you can argue that shields are just as deadly as swords, but there's a reason historically armies which used shields carried an actual weapon do do their killing with. </div> </div> </div>There's a large difference between small scale engagements (aka PCs fighting small groups of opponents) and armies, and how weapons get used. Shields are actual weapons. Armies throughout history had their soldiers carry an array of weapons because one weapon is a horrible way to fight. The gladius, despite it's iconic status, wasn't the original primary 'killing' weapon of the Roman legions (they started with spears in the third line for this), and it's effectiveness was highly dependent on the scutum to control enemy movements and feed them into zones where multiple soldiers could stab at once instead of trying to fight one-on-one like a more common line of troops. They also heavily relied on thrown weapons to soften and disrupt enemy formations (aka kill people) before clinch fighting (shield to shield) began.<br /> <br /> Armies used spears and shields, or swords and shields, etc, because the combination was better than the individual weapons. Shields weren't some afterthought. They were a primary weapon of military combat, and essential to tactics. <br /> <br /> Making this all about shields vs. swords is a fairly annoying line of thought. The point of having multiple weapons is tactical flexibility; in reality and in the game. It's not about sword vs shield, but what weapon is in your other hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shields aren't as effective a weapon as swords. </div> </div> </div>Citation needed, especially as damage in Exalted 3e is not about deadliness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's harder to kill someone with a slab of blunt wood than a pointy metal object. </div> </div> </div>Factually incorrect. Blunt force trauma and penetrating trauma are not directly comparable in terms of how hard it is to kill someone. It's easier to kill someone with a wooden baseball bat than a metal sewing needle, because it's not just about blunt wood vs. pointy metal.<br /> <br /> As well, in the abstraction of the system (which this was a response to) all weapons are equally good at incapacitating people. Again, Damage is about controlling the fight (Initiative), not deadliness. A sword and a shield's only difference in killing people, that is in making Decisive attacks, is in the damage type, not their Damage rating. The Shield Tag reduces Damage rating. Nothing stops me from having a spiked shield, or a shield with a sharpened metal rim, and calling it a Lethal weapon, but it would still be -2 Damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's literally what Charms, Martial Arts and Evocations are for. </div> </div> </div>No, those are for doing cool stuff, not wasting your first few Charms on getting rid of dumb penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T10:18:30-07:00","id":1339398,"title":"","content":"I think the damage penalty is just there to ensure the shield is always paired with another weapon. I'd just houserule that the shield tag doesn't incur a penalty so long as the shield is paired with a non-shield weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T10:22:02-07:00","id":1339399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339384#post1339384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the ability to rapidly advance on an enemy position, protected by the shield so you don't die but somewhat encumbered by the weight?<br /> <br /> Something like being able to Rush without the Defence penalty, but taking -3 to the dice pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rush is only useful against people running away from you. It does nothing to help you advance on an enemy position. Which is why I don't see it used in most fights,* although perhaps that's because I'm not using enough horse archers.<br /> <br /> *Thinking about it... in the 10 games I've run of Lunars, with 2 PCs with Rush charms, I'm not sure I've seen it used at all. Maybe once so the enemy just didn't bother fleeing? No more than once.<br /> <br /> I guess it is a little useful for chasing archers who are running away from you while shooting at you (though you are taking -3 to your Rush rolls), at least once you get to short range (at long or medium range you can't Rush anyway).<br /> Which isn't a very realistic thing for foot archers to do, but they can in Exalted. I guess it's realistic for horse archers to do, but honestly at -3 to your Rush roll if they're on horses I don't think your battle group is likely to succeed on the Rush.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I don't think I'd bother taking the Full Defence action with the 2i cost, -1 Defence and -3 dice, although maybe if you were using something for reducing flurry penalties like you suggested earlier, it works.<br /> <br /> Though this reminds me... can Battle Groups take Full Defence actions? Since they cost 2i.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-04-2019, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T10:23:51-07:00","id":1339400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339353#post1339353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">general negators, basically. Dipping Swallow, Bulwark, Flow Like Blood</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see what you mean, though the -3 to the other action and 2i cost are hefty. Still, +2 non-charm defence is very good.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T11:07:47-07:00","id":1339413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339395#post1339395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, those are for doing cool stuff, not wasting your first few Charms on getting rid of dumb penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wanna be captain america, you need charms. Throwing shields aren't a <i>thing</i> in genre fiction outside of exceptional, heroic, Solar folks. Which is what the Charm quote was referencing.<br /> I have literally no opinon on the rest, I've seen shields used by players who want to do a full defense action and get more oomph out of it. Doesn't seem that bad, but OP--what do you want shields to do?<br /> Making them Light Cover, as some have suggested, actually...seems bad? Since your opponent benefits from the Cover as well(I guess it doesn't cost 2i, but 2i isn't too hefty a cost to me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T11:11:45-07:00","id":1339415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339399#post1339399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though this reminds me... can Battle Groups take Full Defence actions? Since they cost 2i.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen folks Rush to key off charms that benefit from rushing. Anyway, to the Quote--probably? They can pay iniative costs, since they can Engage. I might use it to represent a phalanx or the like (Actually, since no one's mentioned it--does anything stop you from moving and full defensing?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T11:38:27-07:00","id":1339420,"title":"","content":"I see no reason they'd be forbidden to Full Defend. They are forbidden to do Decisives, and their initiative is detached from damage. So you pay the initiative and Defend away. Might be useful while you reload siege weaponry or aim them... but that initiative drop ain't recovering...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T12:52:34-07:00","id":1339426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339395#post1339395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you see to get the core complaint just fine. The Shield Tag isn't good. People want it to not be sub-optimal, instead of just accepting it as sub-optimal and not fixing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I don't get the core complaint. Are you against suboptimal choices in general (in which case I REALLY don't get the core complaint as there are far more egregious balance issues in Exalted like my Axe/Chopping Sword example)? Or is there a specific issue with shields that makes this special which I don't get?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339395#post1339395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A medium shield</div> </div> </div> </div>All published shields are medium. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339395#post1339395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weapon damage is about Initiative</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we have fundementally different interpretations of what Withering damage is and what weapon damage represents. I have no interest in debating this topic but I think it's why we're at loggerheads. I'm gonna drop a quote then park this:<br /> <br /> &quot;To be clear, withering and decisive attacks are a game abstraction used to model the cinematic nature of combat [...] Individuals within the world <br /> of Exalted would recognize no such distinction; [...] characters absolutely intend for most withering attacks to injure or kill their target. [...] Withering attacks must be described as serious combat <br /> maneuvers\u2014they\u2019re usually intended as killing&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339395#post1339395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, those are for doing cool stuff, not wasting your first few Charms on getting rid of dumb penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... ok?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339367#post1339367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or the perspective of doing cool shit like being Exalted Captain America.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-04-2019, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T13:08:47-07:00","id":1339430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339398#post1339398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the damage penalty is just there to ensure the shield is always paired with another weapon. I'd just houserule that the shield tag doesn't incur a penalty so long as the shield is paired with a non-shield weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is this an important consideration though? Why penalize Exalted Captain America? Or some more rare inspirations where a character actually uses two shields?<br /> <br /> If shields were actually really good mechanically, the idea of adding the damage reduction might have some merit. As it stands, it just makes a barely mediocre Tag into a bad one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339413#post1339413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanna be captain america, you need charms. Throwing shields aren't a <i>thing</i> in genre fiction outside of exceptional, heroic, Solar folks. Which is what the Charm quote was referencing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which was missing the original context of why I brought it up and not addressing it. The point, is that the damage penalty on shields doesn't make sense from a simulation stand point, genre emulation, or enabling people to do cool things (which sometimes you need to do for a game; sometimes mundane stuff sucking is how you make cool stuff look awesome).<br /> <br /> The point is that Captain Thunderbolt Shield is objectively worse off than Captain Longfang for the same investment, and there's not good reason for this to be the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since your opponent benefits from the Cover as well(I guess it doesn't cost 2i, but 2i isn't too hefty a cost to me). </div> </div> </div>Only in hand-to-hand. Having the Shield Tag give you Cover would mostly be an anti-ranged attack benefit. Though it's also a good bonus against minor threats that you can hit reliably despite giving them a boost to their Defense, while reducing how much they eat up of your resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339415#post1339415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Actually, since no one's mentioned it--does anything stop you from moving and full defensing?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. You can take your normal Reflexive Move while using Full Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T13:30:27-07:00","id":1339433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339426#post1339426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I don't get the core complaint</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be different from Heavy Arms' (I don't agree with him on some stuff about damage), but personally I just want soldiers with longswords or axes or spears to have some reason to bother carrying shields in their left hands. Currently, I find the benefit to be so marginal that it hardly ever gets used, and in fact people only carry shields because we, OOC, know they ought to, not because the game is giving any real benefit for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T13:50:00-07:00","id":1339440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339426#post1339426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you against suboptimal choices in general (in which case I REALLY don't get the core complaint as there are far more egregious balance issues in Exalted like my Axe/Chopping Sword example)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That there are worse examples doesn't matter, the thread's about the Shield Tag. I house rule the Axe/Chopping Sword thing too. I've been considering redoing the whole base weapon/armor system to something closer to Storypath: get rid of the base stat blocks, and have everything based on Tags with rated Tag to build equipment without creating these sorts of issues (which got easier once Storypath came out and did the math for me).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or is there a specific issue with shields that makes this special which I don't get? </div> </div> </div>There are specific issues with shields as well, mostly that the thing in the setting that's consistently show as using shields the most, have no reasons to use them mechanically: armies. A Small BG defending a commander or sorcerer with shields and a Full Defense + Defender Other combo can at least serve that function. A legion carrying tower shields has no real point to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All published shields are medium. </div> </div> </div>The Shield Tag is not restricted to medium weapons. The writers and developers have simply realized that the Shield Tag is useless or detrimental if your weapon doesn't have a bonus to Parry to it. The Shield Tag was removed from the backer version of the core book from at least one weapon because of this (on a weapon that isn't strictly a shield either), as the Shield Tag doesn't actually work as a general &quot;defensive weapon&quot; Tag. Thus the one mundane and two (IIRC) Artifact shields all being medium weapons doesn't really show much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think we have fundementally different interpretations of what Withering damage is and what weapon damage represents. </div> </div> </div>Possibly, but your arguments so far have been about how much &quot;better&quot; swords are for killing people, with isn't what Withering damage does, or what weapon damage represents. Withering damage dictates who has the tactical advantage in the form of Initiative. Weapon damage represents how good your weapon is at claiming that advantage on a hit. Big heavy weapons don't have high damage just because of how much force they impart when they strike, but because even if an attack with one doesn't impact to deal damage, it's more controlling. It's easier to force someone into an inferior position with a tetsubo than a club. The larger weapon requires moving farther to simply avoid, more energy to block, is more winding as you try to roll with the attack, etc.<br /> <br /> Shield bashes aren't &quot;unserious&quot; attacks. A scutum's boss is meant to break your ribs. A hopolite's heavy round shield's rim is reinforced for being used to break your neck or bash your skull open. Obviously they do more than this, but the point is when someone's using a shield to hit someone, they mean it, just like a sword, or any other weapon. So that part from the book is covered.<br /> <br /> Nothing your saying, whether you want to debate it or not, justifies why the Shield Tag has a damage reduction in it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T15:16:32-07:00","id":1339449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339440#post1339440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. That there are worse examples doesn't matter, the thread's about the Shield Tag.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it's about shields. I think there's a degree of divergence in what we're talking about which is creating real issues in the dialogue.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339433#post1339433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This may be different from Heavy Arms' (I don't agree with him on some stuff about damage), but personally I just want soldiers with longswords or axes or spears to have some reason to bother carrying shields in their left hands. Currently, I find the benefit to be so marginal that it hardly ever gets used, and in fact people only carry shields because we, OOC, know they ought to, not because the game is giving any real benefit for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that specifically an issue with shields? Is there a reason to carry a Chopping Sword in your left hand?<br /> <br /> Offhanding most weapons gives only a marginal advantage, if it gives any advantage at all. The best you can do is a duplicate weapon for Clashes or a Medium weapon (like a Shield) for +1 Parry. Otherwise you're exploring the marginal benefits of tags whereby you give up Grappling and Natural for... whatever.<br /> <br /> If you've got a light weapon (which if we're talking mechanically optimal play rather than rule of cool narrative then you almost certainly have), you're only using the offhand for defence and making all your attacks with your weapon. Which means a tag which increases your defence, if marginally, is objectively better than other options.<br /> <br /> If you're being mechanically suboptimal for the sake of image and using a Medium weapon... and still want a mechanical advantage... then the same logic applies. You take a duplicate weapon. Or you give up Grappling to take a different tag -- and there's one tag that gives a defensive benefit.<br /> <br /> Heavy weapon then you're still going Shield and Lance for the same reasons.<br /> <br /> Thrown weapons offhand are jazzy if you don't have anything better. And I guess it's not inconceivable that you might have weird Charm/Martial Arts investments that make hitting alternate tags viable.<br /> <br /> But if you want a defensive bonus, shields are already the mechanically optimal choice. And we're talking about buffing the best possible option. I'm open to that -- I made my suggestions for the Shield Tag and if you want to add other Tags to Shields, then I'd back Smashing (and be open to Balanced and Flexible if you really want to keep buffing what is already the best option in the game).<br /> <br /> But to address your point: your reason for taking <i>literally the best option in the game</i> for Defensive bonuses is because it is <i>literally the best option in the game</i>. I don't see how you could make shields better at defending people without throwing off the balance. Which then takes you into the realm of using shields for other things, such as offensive weapons -- and clearly that's a direction some people would like to go in. (But I think we've got plenty of offensive options.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-04-2019, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T16:31:23-07:00","id":1339461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339449#post1339449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it's about shields. I think there's a degree of divergence in what we're talking about which is creating real issues in the dialogue.<br /> <br /> Is that specifically an issue with shields? Is there a reason to carry a Chopping Sword in your left hand?<br /> <br /> Offhanding most weapons gives only a marginal advantage, if it gives any advantage at all. The best you can do is a duplicate weapon for Clashes or a Medium weapon (like a Shield) for +1 Parry. Otherwise you're exploring the marginal benefits of tags whereby you give up Grappling and Natural for... whatever.<br /> <br /> If you've got a light weapon (which if we're talking mechanically optimal play rather than rule of cool narrative then you almost certainly have), you're only using the offhand for defence and making all your attacks with your weapon. Which means a tag which increases your defence, if marginally, is objectively better than other options.<br /> <br /> If you're being mechanically suboptimal for the sake of image and using a Medium weapon... and still want a mechanical advantage... then the same logic applies. You take a duplicate weapon. Or you give up Grappling to take a different tag -- and there's one tag that gives a defensive benefit.<br /> <br /> Heavy weapon then you're still going Shield and Lance for the same reasons.<br /> <br /> Thrown weapons offhand are jazzy if you don't have anything better. And I guess it's not inconceivable that you might have weird Charm/Martial Arts investments that make hitting alternate tags viable.<br /> <br /> But if you want a defensive bonus, shields are already the mechanically optimal choice. And we're talking about buffing the best possible option. I'm open to that -- I made my suggestions for the Shield Tag and if you want to add other Tags to Shields, then I'd back Smashing (and be open to Balanced and Flexible if you really want to keep buffing what is already the best option in the game).<br /> <br /> But to address your point: your reason for taking <i>literally the best option in the game</i> for Defensive bonuses is because it is <i>literally the best option in the game</i>. I don't see how you could make shields better at defending people without throwing off the balance. Which then takes you into the realm of using shields for other things, such as offensive weapons -- and clearly that's a direction some people would like to go in. (But I think we've got plenty of offensive options.)</div> </div> </div> </div>*on mobile, so pls forgive formatting errors*<br /> <br /> ... You do realize we *cant* discuss shields without talking about the Shield Tag, right? The Shield Tag is what makes shields mechanically different from *every other melee weapon*.<br /> <br /> In the Rules-As-Written, the Shield Tag makes shields largely inferior as weapons to every other melee weapon....while also giving largely circumstantial and also-largely-shite defensive &quot;bonuses&quot; (that, in pretty much all of the 13+ other threads we have had on why shields suck mechanically, has already been explained in depth). Mechanically-speaking, outside of some *very* circumstantial events, you are just as &quot;protected&quot; by fighting with a sword and dagger than you are with a shield and sword. Which is *nonsense*<br /> <br /> No fighting forces in real life did this. It is so nonsensical as to be comical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T16:43:23-07:00","id":1339465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339461#post1339461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *on mobile, so pls forgive formatting errors*<br /> <br /> ... You do realize we *cant* discuss shields without talking about the Shield Tag, right? The Shield Tag is what makes shields mechanically different from *every other melee weapon*.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right.<br /> <br /> But let's say we keep the Shield Tag as is, but we give shields Balanced, Disarming, Flexible, Grappling, Reaching, Shield, Smashing, Thrown (Long), and Worn?<br /> <br /> Does that change the balance on whether shields are a good thing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339461#post1339461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Rules-As-Written, the Shield Tag makes shields largely inferior as weapons to every other melee weapon....</div> </div> </div> </div>At attacking. Whilst providing the only defensive bonus in the game.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339461#post1339461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while also giving largely circumstantial and also-largely-shite defensive &quot;bonuses&quot; (that, in pretty much all of the 13+ other threads we have had on why shields suck mechanically, has already been explained in depth). Mechanically-speaking, outside of some *very* circumstantial events, you are just as &quot;protected&quot; by fighting with a sword and dagger than you are with a shield and sword. Which is *nonsense*</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted is not built for mortals. Look at what a Difficulty 1 roll represents. Exalted isn't simulationist. Wearing a helmet does nothing, it's a cosmetic choice. Shields are probably great and chamber pots probably exist: but their impact on Exalted is minimal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339461#post1339461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No fighting forces in real life did this. It is so nonsensical as to be comical.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the game where boomerangs were invented to hunt in forests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T17:05:49-07:00","id":1339473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339465#post1339465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right.<br /> <br /> But let's say we keep the Shield Tag as is, but we give shields Balanced, Disarming, Flexible, Grappling, Reaching, Shield, Smashing, Thrown (Long), and Worn?<br /> <br /> Does that change the balance on whether shields are a good thing?<br /> <br /> At attacking. Whilst providing the only defensive bonus in the game.<br /> Exalted is not built for mortals. Look at what a Difficulty 1 roll represents. Exalted isn't simulationist. Wearing a helmet does nothing, it's a cosmetic choice. Shields are probably great and chamber pots probably exist: but their impact on Exalted is minimal.<br /> <br /> In the game where boomerangs were invented to hunt in forests.</div> </div> </div> </div>But...why would we give shields those tags? We already have weapons with those tags, and barring certain irregularities, they work &quot;fine&quot; (for a given sense. I've done a full weapon and tag rewrite before). We arent talking about, say, spears or swords being actively-suboptimal choices, we are talking about shields being actively-suboptimal choices. And to do that, we need to talk about the shield tag.... Since tags are the only differentiation between stat-identical weapons.<br /> <br /> And we have gone over why shields shouldnt have a penalty to attacking, both mechanically and &quot;realistically&quot;. And the RAW shield &quot;bonus&quot; is so circumstantial as to be *irrelevant*, so it obviously isnt a good bonus<br /> <br /> ...you do realize that mortal characters use. *the base mechanics of the entire mechanical setting*, right? And it is *entirely possible* to run 100% mortal stories using the E3 mechanics? I would know, ive done it, multiple times. Asides from the shittiness of the Shield Tag (and, therefore, shields as weapons), E3 is by far the best Exalted editions for running mortal campaigns.<br /> <br /> Hell, it can be argued that the base settings are *for* mortals, since Exalted dont have to deal with disease, bleeding, etc.<br /> <br /> And, as an aside, if a house has a shitty foundation, dont expect it to stand very long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T22:29:35-07:00","id":1339526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339465#post1339465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that change the balance on whether shields are a good thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It's just an example of why the original Devs deciding to have Tag assignments as &quot;whatever you think fits&quot; without any mechanical constraints was a bad decision.<br /> <br /> The Shield Tag still sucks, even if you put in on a weapon with a dozen good Tags.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whilst providing the only defensive bonus in the game. </div> </div> </div>1) It's not the only defensive bonus available in the game, nor is it even a bonus to Defense itself. It isn't actually a bonus to defense at all, it's an increase in options for Flurries.<br /> <br /> 2) It only has any benefit at all with weapons that have a Parry bonus of +1 or higher. The +1 Parry from medium weapons is the only true defensive bonus in the base stats and tags of weapons. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exalted is not built for mortals. </div> </div> </div>There's rules for playing them in the core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wearing a helmet does nothing, it's a cosmetic choice. Shields are probably great and chamber pots probably exist: but their impact on Exalted is minimal. </div> </div> </div>If the game wanted shields to be in the same category as helmets, there shouldn't be a Shield Tag, or a shield weapon, and it should have been abstracted out like helmets are. By making shields a thing that counts in the system, it should have an impact on the game; Exalted included.<br /> <br /> By having the stat block and the Tag, a shield is meant to matter to Exalted (the game and the characters) as much as any other weapon and tag deeply associated with that weapon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T01:39:21-07:00","id":1339548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339449#post1339449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it's about shields. I think there's a degree of divergence in what we're talking about which is creating real issues in the dialogue.<br /> <br /> Is that specifically an issue with shields? Is there a reason to carry a Chopping Sword in your left hand?</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that no line infantry historically was working around with a slashing sword in one hand and a chopping sword in the other, so I don't really care if no-one in Exalted is doing it.<br /> <br /> Whereas I would like a battle group of Harborheadian soldiers (who I always imagine like Zulu warriors, ie short spears and big cowhide shields) to have some bonus for carrying shields (or penalty for not having shields) because if they've got one-handed spears in one hand, there ought to be a reason for them to also carry shields rather than just wave their left hand around doing nothing.<br /> <br /> The clash bonus you suggested earlier would be okay. I'd prefer something different to having two swords, but it would be okay.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T01:42:06-07:00","id":1339550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339465#post1339465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the game where boomerangs were invented to hunt in forests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this did give me a chuckle.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I think that, while it's fair to say &quot;this isn't a 100% simulationist game, because genre&quot;, I don't think that necessarily leads to &quot;shield/longsword or shield/axe should be rubbish choice that people won't bother with&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T01:45:50-07:00","id":1339551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339526#post1339526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) It's not the only defensive bonus available in the game, nor is it even a bonus to Defense itself. It isn't actually a bonus to defense at all, it's an increase in options for Flurries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't think &quot;an increase in Defence&quot; is an utterly terrible way of describing it, if very reductive.<br /> <br /> It lets you take penalties to your Rush/Disengage and pay 2i to get +1 Defence while Rushing/Disengaging.<br /> <br /> Maybe &quot;It gives you an expensive Defence boost when Rushing/Disengaging&quot; is the best description.<br /> <br /> (I suspect the bonus when Disengaging is more useful than the bonus when Rushing, but at that point you're spending 4i, which is a lot, not to mention it decreases the chance of getting away.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T03:10:56-07:00","id":1339555,"title":"","content":"My point is more that it doesn't give you a +1 Defense, it gives you a +1 net Defense from using Full Defense in a Flurry with some actions (you can technically use it to Flurry Full Defense + Draw Weapon, it's just completely pointless to do so since Draw Weapon hits you with another -1 Defense, and your total net becomes +0 Defense for 2i).<br /> <br /> The best description would be that it gives you an expensive effective Defense boost for some of the Flurries it allows you do to; namely Defend Other and movement actions. The fact that it's written to allow you to literally pay Initiative for no benefit if you use it wrong is worth remembering when discussing it's design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T03:35:45-07:00","id":1339558,"title":"","content":"I assume you mean the no benefit of using it with Draw Weapon? Because you do have a benefit, you're ignoring the penalty to draw your weapon.<br /> <br /> Although that requires you to have drawn your shield, and you could instead maybe have drawn a longsword... but I think there's good reasons to have your shield strapped to your arm but not your sword out. It's less threatening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T09:26:31-07:00","id":1339614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339473#post1339473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But...why would we give shields those tags?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Heavy Arms at least thinks shields are great weapons for controlling the flow of battle. Knocking people over with your shield (Smashing), doing extra damage (Overwhelming), and Captain America style hijinks (Thrown) play into that.<br /> <br /> Is there a reason why everything a shield does should be tied to the shield tag?<br /> <br /> As I pointed out, the primary benefit of shields is that they are Medium weapons and thus give +1 Parry. That's nothing to do with the shield tag. Whether or not you should offhand a shield with your whip, or take a slashing sword has been argued <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339367#post1339367\">in this thread</a> in terms of the sword having more favourable tags.<br /> <br /> Axes aren't defined by having the Axe tag -- and they do more than just make Chopping attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339473#post1339473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've done a full weapon and tag rewrite before).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you feel that fixes shields, I'd love to see it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339473#post1339473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We arent talking about, say, spears or swords being actively-suboptimal choices, we are talking about shields being actively-suboptimal choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about shields being suboptimal <i>relative</i> to spears or swords. In terms of pure defence, I'm arguing they're not suboptimal -- but the value of defence in Exalted is questionable. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339473#post1339473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we have gone over why shields shouldnt have a penalty to attacking, both mechanically and &amp;quot;realistically&amp;quot;. And the RAW shield &amp;quot;bonus&amp;quot; is so circumstantial as to be *irrelevant*, so it obviously isnt a good bonus</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't think that's kind of axiomatic?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339473#post1339473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...you do realize that mortal characters use. *the base mechanics of the entire mechanical setting*, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A lot of rules in Exalted, especially the combat engine, are heavy abstractions rather than faithful simulations.&quot;<br /> <br /> The rules for Parry on QCs refers to &quot;excellent shields&quot;, battle-ready troops and Brides of Ahlat use shields.<br /> <br /> What value items have to mortal heroes is not a faithful simulation of the value to mortals within the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T10:59:09-07:00","id":1339637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339526#post1339526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's rules for playing them in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't change the fact that the rules are not built for them. See, for example, the Martial Artist Merit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T13:03:36-07:00","id":1339684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339558#post1339558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you mean the no benefit of using it with Draw Weapon? Because you do have a benefit, you're ignoring the penalty to draw your weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which... would have happened if you just used the passive +1 bonus for a medium weapon, from any medium weapon, anyway.<br /> <br /> And remember your first draw action in normal combat is free when combat starts. You don't have to walk around with any weapon readied all the time. Unless you get ambushed, pulling our your sword, or getting your shield on, are both things you can do before anything in the fight actually happens. It's drawing a second weapon that comes with consideration of needing an action in combat to pull off.<br /> <br /> Nothing presents Exalted in as general as a sense as this could be applied, where having a shield readied in your hands as you're just going about your daily business as something people would treat as normal and non-aggressive, even if less aggressive than a drawn sword. Shields are combat weapons, it's not like staff or baton that you could claim is a walking aid to just have in your hands openly all the time; even a tool knife is something you sheath when you're not using it, rather than just carrying it around in the open if you're looking to not cause a social scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339614#post1339614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Heavy Arms at least thinks shields are great weapons for controlling the flow of battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>In reference to their damage rating. Is, &quot;I'm going to show them by making obviously bad faith arguments!&quot; something you're doing consciously?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there a reason why everything a shield does should be tied to the shield tag? </div> </div> </div>This already isn't actually the case, but because of the Shield Tag, the only useful thing a shield has the majority of the time is being a medium weapon and getting the +1 Parry from that all medium weapons get, so the Shield Tag needs to both not get in the way of other options (the damage reduction on attacks, chopping swords and axes don't have to deal with a penalty for not making a chopping attack and just using normal ones), and actually do something because be a medium weapon to get a +1 Defense that's worth using.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're talking about shields being suboptimal <i>relative</i> to spears or swords. In terms of pure defence, I'm arguing they're not suboptimal -- but the value of defence in Exalted is questionable. </div> </div> </div>Well, we're talking about plenty of things besides this specific thing.<br /> <br /> Your arguments about them being not suboptimal don't hold up:<br /> <br /> 1) Non-medium shields using Full Defense + Flurry are either equal to the passive bonus of a medium weapon, but cost Initiative to use, making them worse, or less than the passive bonus of a medium weapon and still cost you initiative to use, making the even worse.<br /> <br /> 2) Using shields to do Full Defense + Flurry can net you a +1 Defense, but costs you Initiative, and can't be used in combination with attacks, so you can't strike back to regain that Initiative. You're bleeding yourself dry until you can't use Full Defense any more without Crashing yourself and making it easier for your opponents to Crash you once you stop being on the defensive.<br /> <br /> The value of Defense in Exalted 3e isn't questionable. Every attempt to crunch the numbers points out that the medium stat block is actually the most optimal stat block because of the +1 Parry. It negates light weapons having an accuracy advantage while maintaining a damage advantage (meaning they're strike about the same number of times, but medium does more damage on average, giving it the edge), and the extra damage of heavy weapons is overcome by the disparity in hit-rates (though a bit more even with artifact weapons).<br /> <br /> What's questionable are paying Initiative to boost Defense against Withering attacks at all (normal Full Defense against Decisive attacks is definitely valuable), and paying Initiative to reduce your maximum Defense to perform another action along side your Full Defense while facing a Decisive attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't think that's kind of axiomatic? </div> </div> </div>The fact that we've explained what we see as the flaws in the Shield Tag means it's not axiomatic even if you disagree with those arguments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What value items have to mortal heroes is not a faithful simulation of the value to mortals within the setting. </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't justify shields being shitty weapons any more than it justifies the suboptimal axes vs. chopping swords thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339637#post1339637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which doesn't change the fact that the rules are not built for them. See, for example, the Martial Artist Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your example doesn't explain anything.<br /> <br /> The Martial Artist Merit is a gating mechanism because the developers felt it was necessary to create one. The game was built for you to take this Merit, as well as make martial artist characters. The fact that the Merit is oriented around Exalts is definitely a flaw in the Merit (one that's not really hard to solve without breaking the designers' goal: make it necessary before you can buy MA Charms rather than MA Abilities, boom, done), but the flaw is mostly there because the original developers wanted mundane martial arts to do more, but couldn't figure out how without breaking things once Exalts get involved.<br /> <br /> You can't validily claim the rules aren't built for something that's built into the game. You can question if that was a good decision on the designers' part, but Death of the Author doesn't apply here even if you like to apply it. The game was built for shields to be a thing that count. That's undeniable because the game was built to make shields a thing that counts by making them a thing that counts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T13:38:17-07:00","id":1339691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339684#post1339684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which... would have happened if you just used the passive +1 bonus for a medium weapon, from any medium weapon, anyway.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to John's point about flurrying Full Defence and Draw Weapon, which you can only do with Shields. That gives you +1 Defence for 2i, cancelling out the penalty for Drawing a weapon (and the -3 penalty to rolls is irrelevant). I'm just saying he's technically correct there.<br /> <br /> But while John is technically right there, I think this is generally not something that's going to get used all that much (as you mentioned later in the post). Same with flurrying Full Defence and Rush or Disengage, which I haven't seen anyone bother to do. I don't think people generally consider 2i and -3 on a roll that worth it for +1 Defence, so giving people the option to do so isn't that useful.<br /> <br /> If we took John's idea of ignoring the Defence penalty from Flurrying, it becomes more attractive, 2i is decent for +2 Defence I think. But for me, the benefit only applying to Rush/Disengage/Draw/Misc actions isn't something that either a)I expect to come up a lot, or b)fits with my vision of Realm soldiers in tetsudo fighting barbarians in a shield wall (where any man not holding a shield would, in real life, be in deep trouble, but in Exalted it makes no difference and they might as well not have shields at all).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about shields being suboptimal <i>relative</i> to spears or swords.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you should be. No-one fights with a shield and nothing else.<br /> <br /> The argument is medium spear/sword+medium shield vs medium spear/sword+light weapon (knife, hand, etc) vs 2 medium swords.<br /> <br /> (I think we all agree that short sword+medium shield is a great combination, there's no issue there, for anyone with a short sword taking a shield is a very attractive choice.)<br /> <br /> Hmmm... do off-hand penalties apply to your Defence pool? Or just actions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T14:16:12-07:00","id":1339697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339684#post1339684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In reference to their damage rating. Is, &quot;I'm going to show them by making obviously bad faith arguments!&quot; something you're doing consciously?</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully concede that your post was in reference to the Damage rating. Do you not feel like Tags like Smashing could represent battlefield control?<br /> <br /> You made a post extolling the virtues of using a shield to control the battlefield, I made a post explaining how this could be represented via Tags and explained my reasoning. That's a discussion, not bad faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339684#post1339684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This already isn't actually the case, but because of the Shield Tag, the only useful thing a shield has the majority of the time is being a medium weapon and getting the +1 Parry from that all medium weapons get, so the Shield Tag needs to both not get in the way of other options (the damage reduction on attacks, chopping swords and axes don't have to deal with a penalty for not making a chopping attack and just using normal ones), and actually do something because be a medium weapon to get a +1 Defense that's worth using.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shields are primarily useful because they get +1 Parry. As a concious design choice, they are not designed to be wielded in a pair of shields, or used as a primary weapon. The shield tag increases the defensive benefits of using a shield.<br /> <br /> Conversely, Chopping is worse than Piercing and an Axe is straight up better than a Chopping Sword.<br /> <br /> If I have a Javelin in one hand, then having an Axe in the other opens up more offensive options and no defensive options. Having a Chopping Sword in the offhand offers objectively fewer offensive options and no defensive options. Having a Shield offers no offensive options but the Shield Tag is the only Tag in the game which offers defensive options. <br /> <br /> The Shield Tag offers a means for increasing Defence on a weapon designed for defence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339684#post1339684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we're talking about plenty of things besides this specific thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happy to address them if you want to highlight them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339684#post1339684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your arguments about them being not suboptimal don't hold up:<br /> <br /> 1) Non-medium shields</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't exist. If your homebrew is causing problems that don't exist in the default setting, then maybe the default setting isn't to blame for your problems?<br /> <br /> I've covered this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339684#post1339684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Using shields to do Full Defense + Flurry can net you a +1 Defense, but costs you Initiative, and can't be used in combination with attacks, so you can't strike back to regain that Initiative. You're bleeding yourself dry until you can't use Full Defense any more without Crashing yourself and making it easier for your opponents to Crash you once you stop being on the defensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is specifically why I stated defence was of questionable value. Likewise the Chopping Tag lowers your Defence, making it easier to bleed out Initative, and costs Initative in order to marginally increase gains on a successful attack.<br /> <br /> Neither Tag is useless, but both are situational.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339684#post1339684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The value of Defense in Exalted 3e isn't questionable. Every attempt to crunch the numbers points out that the medium stat block is actually the most optimal stat block because of the +1 Parry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a great argument for pairing a shield with your short sword. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339684#post1339684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's questionable are paying Initiative to boost Defense against Withering attacks at all (normal Full Defense against Decisive attacks is definitely valuable), and paying Initiative to reduce your maximum Defense to perform another action along side your Full Defense while facing a Decisive attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Questionable? Yes.<br /> <br /> Situationally useful? Also yes.<br /> <br /> Granted by any other non-magical means? No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339684#post1339684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that we've explained what we see as the flaws in the Shield Tag means it's not axiomatic even if you disagree with those arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your arguments are logical and I see your point of view. You think the Shield Tag is a problem because it reduces the amount of Damage shields do and you don't value the benefits of the Tag. (I hope you don't view that summary as &quot;bad faith&quot; -- I'm happy to edit if you want to clarify.) Because you hold this point of view, you'd like to see shields buffed.<br /> <br /> I don't agree with your point of view and ergo I don't think shields need to be buffed. I'm happy to provide my input into this conversation, and suggest shield buffs that don't upset the mechanical balance of the game. But I'm unconvinced by your argument that shields are &quot;bad&quot;. I think shields are good. Simply restating your argument and framing the discussion as if your position is true is what I mean by taking an &quot;axiomatic&quot; position in this discussion. I'm happy to engage with you as if your position is true (even though I think you're objectively and demonstratably wrong), and I have posted numerous suggestions as to how I think shields could be buffed. You're free to ignore my suggestions, of course, and I'm eager to read the ideas of others. But I'm having great fun with a shield <i>as is</i> -- I'm not saying &quot;you're doing it wrong&quot; or &quot;don't try to make the game better&quot;, but I am saying &quot;check your premises&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339684#post1339684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which doesn't justify shields being shitty weapons any more than it justifies the suboptimal axes vs. chopping swords thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you consider it a problem if shields did full damage and gave +2 Parry?<br /> <br /> If you would, then go back and reread my post.<br /> If you wouldn't, then there's your homebrew solution -- enjoy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-05-2019, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T14:20:05-07:00","id":1339699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339691#post1339691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to John's point about flurrying Full Defence and Draw Weapon, which you can only do with Shields.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... I'm not sure which point you're talking about. Unless I'm being very selective in my reading, I've been the only one to talk about Flurrying Full Defense with stuff besides Rush/Disengage/Defend Other<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmmm... do off-hand penalties apply to your Defence pool? Or just actions? </div> </div> </div>Just actions from how things are written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T14:31:28-07:00","id":1339702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339691#post1339691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you should be. No-one fights with a shield and nothing else.<br /> <br /> The argument is medium spear/sword+medium shield vs medium spear/sword+light weapon (knife, hand, etc) vs 2 medium swords.<br /> <br /> (I think we all agree that short sword+medium shield is a great combination, there's no issue there, for anyone with a short sword taking a shield is a very attractive choice.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I was being unclear, but this is what I meant.<br /> <br /> Though I think it's worth my expressly saying I don't think fighting with a shield on its own, or with two shields, should be a fighting style which doesn't have drawbacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339691#post1339691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... do off-hand penalties apply to your Defence pool? Or just actions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Word of Vance is that it doesn't, but RAW it's a penalty so it subtracts directly from the static value, not the pool. (Ambidextrous implies it only effects Actions but Tail refers to off-hand as a general Penality.) I think that given the text of Ambidextrous and WoV, the RAI is clearly that it's just actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T14:45:28-07:00","id":1339705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339699#post1339699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... I'm not sure which point you're talking about. Unless I'm being very selective in my reading, I've been the only one to talk about Flurrying Full Defense with stuff besides Rush/Disengage/Defend Other</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say &quot;selective&quot; as such, but I this I meant by divergence in the dialogue. <br /> <br /> You and Wizard are both reading into what I've written and working what you think I've said into the discussion. Wizard has correctly inferred what I've been implying and has related that to what you've expressly said (and I've seen no reason to repeat myself), whilst you've inferred something different (which is no poor reflection on yourself -- you can only read what I've wrote) and we've ended up having two very different conversations. It happens.<br /> <br /> Wizard and I started this discussion in our first posts in this thread. But for clarity:<br /> <br /> One of the advantages of using a shield is flurrying Draw/Ready with Full Defence.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> What do y'all think of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339543-exalted-3e-weapon-revision\">this</a>? I think it's pretty well balanced. Little bit of weirdness but I think it handles shields well relative to other options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-05-2019, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T15:48:22-07:00","id":1339717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339697#post1339697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you not feel like Tags like Smashing could represent battlefield control?</div> </div> </div> </div>Smashing is certainly a tag that could or even should be applied to some shields.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I made a post explaining how this could be represented via Tags and explained my reasoning. </div> </div> </div>No, you didn't. If you intend this, you epic failed at it.<br /> <br /> What you did, was make a post that asked if shields would be fixed by giving them a bunch of tags instead of fixing the Shield Tag, which is a bad faith argument that dismisses and misrepresents what people are saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shields are primarily useful because they get +1 Parry. </div> </div> </div>Except there's no reason to use a shield because they don't get a +1 Parry for being a shield. This is a reason to keep a medium weapon in your off-hand if your primary weapon is one-handed. Any other medium weapon is a better choice because you could get tags that are more useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a concious design choice, they are not designed to be wielded in a pair of shields, or used as a primary weapon. </div> </div> </div>There's nothing stopping either of these, it's just suboptimal. By this logic axes were consciously designed to be superior to chopping swords, and we shouldn't change that either.<br /> <br /> So either we agree sub-optimal stuff should be removed, or not. I don't care about these appeals to the text. If you think addressing things like the axe vs. chopping sword thing is worth doing, then appealing to the way the text was written doesn't work. If you want to talk about ways to address it, that would be different, but you've been arguing against fixing shields this whole time instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The shield tag increases the defensive benefits of using a shield. </div> </div> </div>It increases the options you have in a Flurry, which sometimes provides a defensive benefit, and sometimes it doesn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conversely, Chopping is worse than Piercing... </div> </div> </div>This is far more situational. Chopping's Withering benefit doesn't depend on your target wearing armor, just on your ability not to get reduced to ping damage, and it has a decisive bonus which Piercing doesn't. Though I find the cost of a lot of &quot;active&quot; Tags to be too high and thus largely avoided by players..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I have a javelin in one hand, then having an Axe in the other opens up more offensive options and no defensive options. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't increase your Defense. You have a defensive option in using range to avoid a close range attack completely as you have two throwable weapons, and you don't lose the +1 Parry for throwing either weapon like you would if you mixed medium and light weapons instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Shield Tag offers a means for increasing Defence on a weapon designed for defence. </div> </div> </div>The Full Defense action was already available to your character with or without the shield. The shield allows you to Flurry it, which reduces the benefit of Full Defense inherently, and possibly more depending on what other action you use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm happy to address them if you want to highlight them. </div> </div> </div>Is this a change from your previous statement?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't exist. </div> </div> </div>Does the book:<br /> <br /> 1) Say they can't exist.<br /> <br /> 2) Say that the weapons in the core book are an exhaustive list of weapons in the setting, and any weapon that isn't listed should be fit to these stats.<br /> <br /> If no to both of these, how would you represent shields that don't fit the existing shield stat block, as shields are more varied than one permutation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your homebrew is causing problems that don't exist in the default setting, then maybe the default setting isn't to blame for your problems? </div> </div> </div>Applying the shield tag to non-medium weapons is something that should model things that exist in the setting. Tower shields (specifically the Roman style scutum) explicitly exist in the setting, and don't match the description or stats of the base-line shield in the core book.<br /> <br /> Also, as has been addressed before, shields as mainly a weapon of armies and how the Shield Tag interacts with BGs is also something where the default setting is at odds with the rules, not some issue with homebrew.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've covered this. </div> </div> </div>And I've covered why it is not a meaningful counterpoint before too. So repeating yourself without making a new point of it doesn't really mean anything new.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise the Chopping Tag lowers your Defence, making it easier to bleed out Initative, and costs Initative in order to marginally increase gains on a successful attack. </div> </div> </div>Chopping is a gamble where you put up Init in the hopes of getting more out of it than you put in. The odds aren't great, but there's risk and potential reward.<br /> <br /> In terms of Initiative Shield's Full Defense Flurry is paying to gamble on how much you lose, with no inherent ability to gain from it. You can't even break even, you will lose Initiative. The potential rewards are in the other action you take succeeding at all, and if so being able to dig you out of the hole you've already dug yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Neither Tag is useless, but both are situational. </div> </div> </div>Basically? The shield Tag is situational in a fashion that doesn't actually help it be a fun &quot;shield&quot; in terms of actually playing the game as a character that wants to sword and board instead of other options. If your goal is to build a &quot;tank&quot; character, shields have nothing for you that any other medium weapon doesn't already provide (and you'll want things like the +2 Clash bonus if you don't care too much about a lot of Tags).<br /> <br /> The math on Chopping might be a trap, but you at least get the thrill of risking and going for broke with it.<br /> <br /> Shield might not be useless, but that doesn't mean it's good for making shields perform as people that want their characters to have shields would want them to perform. And usefulness isn't binary. Chopping and Shield can have major issues, but that doesn't mean they're equal in this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Granted by any other non-magical means? No. </div> </div> </div>Cover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ..and you don't value the benefits of the Tag. </div> </div> </div>I don't consider the value of the benefits of the Tag sufficient for the cost. The idea of being able to Flurry Full Defense isn't bad, the RAW execution of it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because you hold this point of view, you'd like to see shields buffed. </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> I want two things:<br /> <br /> 1) Defensive weapons that don't rely on a +1 Parry bonus inherent to the medium weapon stat block to be effective, so light and heavy defensive weapons are viable.<br /> <br /> 2) Shields that function more like how shields function in inspirational sources; especially making sure they're useful for BGs.<br /> <br /> I think the basic shield in the book should probably have the Smashing Tag, but that's a minor issue compared to fixing the Shield Tag; which I feel is best done by dividing it into two Tags. One Tag to handle the Flurry part and do something with Clashes. One Tag to use Cover as the primary defensive bonus, as Cover is a mixed blessing isn't less of a buff and more of a different way to getting to a similar result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simply restating your argument and framing the discussion as if your position is true is axiomatic. </div> </div> </div>Your entire approach to this conversation so far can be summed up as, &quot;Shields are good is an axiomatic truth, therefore as long as I post something, it should be treated as automatically proving arguments that shields aren't good as successful no matter how poor the logic behind it.&quot;<br /> <br /> It would be easier to interpret your posts in a better light if you didn't mix these attempts to return to something productive with this sort of projection happy nonsense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (even though I think you're objectively and demonstratably wrong) </div> </div> </div>And yet, you can't demonstrate it successfully....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and I have posted numerous suggestions as to how I think shields could be buffed. </div> </div> </div>Most of which come off as condescending and bad faith, because they're phrased as rhetorical attacks rather than actually engaging with the positions of people dissatisfied with shields RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....but I am saying &quot;check your premises&quot;. </div> </div> </div>My premises are just fine, thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you consider it a problem if shields did full damage and gave +2 Parry? </div> </div> </div>Yes, because a flat +2 Parry is bad for the game, the +1 Parry on medium weapons is already questionable for the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you would, then go back and reread my post. </div> </div> </div>Nothing in your post resolves this.<br /> <br /> And again, this doesn't come off as an honest attempt at a suggestion, it just comes off as a rhetorical mislead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T17:43:04-07:00","id":1339732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339705#post1339705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do y'all think of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339543-exalted-3e-weapon-revision\">this</a>? I think it's pretty well balanced. Little bit of weirdness but I think it handles shields well relative to other options.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a good baseline to allow players to fix shields however they want.<br /> <br /> For instance you could add these tags :<br /> <br /> -<b>Light/Heavy Cover</b> (1-2) : you can use this weapon to take Light / Heavy Cover (moving ends the effect). If this weapon has the Shield Tag, taking cover behind this weapon can be placed in a Flurry.<br /> -<b>Protective</b> (1) : +1 Parry (cannot be added to Medium Weapons)<br /> <br /> -<b>Medium/Heavy Weight</b> (1-2) : -1 / -2 mobility penalty<br /> -<b>Defensive</b> (-2) : -2 Damage (the rework removes the -2 penalty on shields, this tag brings it back)<br /> -<b>Obstructing</b> (-1) : -1 to vision based Awareness<br /> <br /> <br /> And then you can have these shields :<br /> <br /> <b>Large Shield</b> (Medium) - Melee, Bashing, Shield, Worn, Smashing, Light Cover, Medium Weight, Defensive<br /> <br /> <b>Tower Shield</b> (Heavy) - Melee, Bashing, Shield, Worn, Smashing, Heavy Cover, Protective, Heavy Weight, Defensive, Obstructing<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 10-05-2019, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T18:22:55-07:00","id":1339735,"title":"","content":"As I noted earlier in the thread, I think moving towards Storypath's method solves a lot of problems, though I'm not sure I'd use that specific implementation and that should be discussed there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T19:24:34-07:00","id":1339744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339735#post1339735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I noted earlier in the thread, I think moving towards Storypath's method solves a lot of problems, though I'm not sure I'd use that specific implementation and that should be discussed there.</div> </div> </div> </div>My suggestion stands on its own, feel free to ignore that the 2 shields were made using the other thread's system and simply look at their effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T01:46:57-07:00","id":1339784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Smashing is certainly a tag that could or even should be applied to some shields.<br /> <br /> No, you didn't. If you intend this, you epic failed at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to refer you <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339614#post1339614\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you did, was make a post that asked if shields would be fixed by giving them a bunch of tags instead of fixing the Shield Tag, which is a bad faith argument that dismisses and misrepresents what people are saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to represent what other people are saying. I'm making my point that Shields (the weapon) are more than the Shield Tag. A point which you seem not to be able to grasp. I'm suggesting using the existing system to fix your perceived problem rather than venture into homebrew and...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the basic shield in the book should probably have the Smashing Tag, but that's a minor issue compared to fixing the Shield Tag; which I feel is best done by dividing it into two Tags. One Tag to handle the Flurry part and do something with Clashes. One Tag to use Cover as the primary defensive bonus, as Cover is a mixed blessing isn't less of a buff and more of a different way to getting to a similar result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey look at that, it's actually a valid point you agree with at least somewhat.<br /> <br /> To address your main complaint: if that's the way you want to fix shields then go for it. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339247#post1339247\">Your original post stands on its own merit, and I have nothing further to add -- which is why I never replied to it.</a> I have no interest in giving you further feedback on your idea but if it works for you then I'm happy for you. Perhaps you'd enjoy feedback from DrLoveMonkey who posted the same idea before you joined the thread?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except there's no reason to use a shield because they don't get a +1 Parry for being a shield. This is a reason to keep a medium weapon in your off-hand if your primary weapon is one-handed. Any other medium weapon is a better choice because you could get tags that are more useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I have an Axe in one hand, the marginal benefits of a shield in the other, in that it allows me to Flurry Full Defence, is more useful than holding a Chopping Sword with redundant Tags.<br /> <br /> You are making value statements as if they were axiomatic truths. They aren't. I'm not going to respond to this argument further.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing stopping either of these, it's just suboptimal. By this logic axes were consciously designed to be superior to chopping swords, and we shouldn't change that either.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've found the point.<br /> <br /> In Exalted, since 1st Ed, as in real life some weapons are better than others. Exalted's combat system is designed as an abstraction to allow players to make interesting choices about their characters, but much of that choice is aesthetic.<br /> <br /> If you're arguing &quot;all weapons should be balanced&quot;, then you need to rework the system -- such as the homebrew I linked above, or 2E's DE Armory Homebrew.<br /> <br /> If you're arguing weapons should be unbalanced but shields should be better, then I don't get why. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339384#post1339384\">As I said ages ago</a>.<br /> <br /> If you're not interested in a rework approach and want to strictly discuss shields in the framework of a balance which doesn't exist, then I can't help you.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So either we agree sub-optimal stuff should be removed, or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do not. I haven't said sub-optimal stuff should be removed: I've said Shields are already optimal, Shields are more than the Shield Tag, and weapons are inherently unbalanced. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't care about these appeals to the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot read this any other way than &quot;I don't care about the published rules of the game&quot;. And <i>that</i> might be bad faith on my part, but if that's not your point then I'm asking you to clarify.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to talk about ways to address it, that would be different, but you've been arguing against fixing shields this whole time instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339182#post1339182\">If only I'd made...</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339384#post1339384\">posts in this thread...</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339465#post1339465\">on how to fix shields...</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339614#post1339614\">then I wouldn't look foolish.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339705#post1339705\">(And sharing the ideas of others.)</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It increases the options you have in a Flurry, which sometimes provides a defensive benefit, and sometimes it doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>When does including Full Defence in your Flurry not have a defensive benefit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Full Defense action was already available to your character with or without the shield. The shield allows you to Flurry it, which reduces the benefit of Full Defense inherently, and possibly more depending on what other action you use.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rush action is available inherently <s>and it reduces your Defence</s>. Shields let you Rush (and perform numerous other actions) <s>without lowering your defence</s> with an improved defence (or a reduced penalty in the case of using other actions).<br /> <br /> It's not about doing something else to reduce the benefit of Full Defence. It's about using a shield to ameliorate defensive penalties or increase your defences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a change from your previous statement?</div> </div> </div> </div>No? Which statement? The one where I claimed to understand your complaint?<br /> <br /> If you think the issue with shields is not their worth relative to other weapons, then I'm willing to debate this with you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the book:<br /> <br /> 1) Say they can't exist.<br /> <br /> 2) Say that the weapons in the core book are an exhaustive list of weapons in the setting, and any weapon that isn't listed should be fit to these stats.<br /> <br /> If no to both of these, how would you represent shields that don't fit the existing shield stat block, as shields are more varied than one permutation.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Tags and narrative description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Applying the shield tag to non-medium weapons is something that should model things that exist in the setting. Tower shields (specifically the Roman style scutum) explicitly exist in the setting, and don't match the description or stats of the base-line shield in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd straight up use the normal Shield stats and model other benefits/penalities with Stunts, Strategems and Command actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as has been addressed before, shields as mainly a weapon of armies and how the Shield Tag interacts with BGs is also something where the default setting is at odds with the rules, not some issue with homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, I'd highlight that the rules exist to showcase exceptional heroes, not rank and file. That the system is an abstraction, not a simulation. And that battlegroups are almost certainly Quick Characters and their stats should thus be synthesized to fit the story rather than strictly derived like a PC's.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of Initiative Shield's Full Defense Flurry is paying to gamble on how much you lose, with no inherent ability to gain from it. You can't even break even, you will lose Initiative. The potential rewards are in the other action you take succeeding at all, and if so being able to dig you out of the hole you've already dug yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't Flurry Take Cover with Rush or Disengage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shield might not be useless, but that doesn't mean it's good for making shields perform as people that want their characters to have shields would want them to perform.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> I don't consider the value of the benefits of the Tag sufficient for the cost. The idea of being able to Flurry Full Defense isn't bad, the RAW execution of it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a valid opinion. And I'm keen to help people who have this opinion to have more fun. I'm willing to suggest improvements and point out the ideas of others.<br /> <br /> But it's not my opinion. Nor is it an objective truth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your entire approach to this conversation so far can be summed up as, &quot;Shields are good is an axiomatic truth, therefore as long as I post something, it should be treated as automatically proving arguments that shields aren't good as successful no matter how poor the logic behind it.&quot;<br /> <br /> It would be easier to interpret your posts in a better light if you didn't mix these attempts to return to something productive with this sort of projection happy nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the first post I made in this thread. Then come back and apologise to me.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, shields are good. I'm open to other points of view and have suggested improvements for how to make shields better.<br /> <br /> What you call &quot;projection happy nonsense&quot; is civility. You've frankly exhausted mine.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to engage with my argument then don't. I came to this thread, suggested how shields could be improved then gave my opinion on RAW. Every single post I've made since has been a direct reply to someone addressing my points.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of which come off as condescending and bad faith, because they're phrased as rhetorical attacks rather than actually engaging with the positions of people dissatisfied with shields RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a reductionist and willful misrepresentation of my position: i.e. bad faith.<br /> <br /> If you want to ignore my argument then do so, but cease the charade of engaging in a discussion (bound by the rules of this forum).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339717#post1339717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My premises are just fine, thank you.<br /> <br /> Yes, because a flat +2 Parry is bad for the game, the +1 Parry on medium weapons is already questionable for the game.<br /> <br /> Nothing in your post resolves this.<br /> <br /> And again, this doesn't come off as an honest attempt at a suggestion, it just comes off as a rhetorical mislead.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is simple: where two people have different opinions on an issue they're going to have two different solutions. If you want to flat buff shields, you can just give them +1 Parry. It's a serious suggestion. And if your only concern is making Shields better then it's not bad-wrong-fun -- go with my blessing and have fun.<br /> <br /> Why is it not a good idea? I said: because Exalted is an abstraction that allows you to make interesting decisions about your character. Making shields too good makes the decision less interesting and wonks the math behind the abstraction. So, check your premises.<br /> <br /> If a +1 Parry on Medium weapons is bad for the game, you need to do more than fix the Shield Tag to fix Shields. And you need to do more to Equipment than fix Shields. Which changes the scope of the discussion.<br /> <br /> If you're after some kind of balance system wise, which expressly and deliberately does not exist in Exalted, nor has it ever existed in Exalted, then, again, you need a wider discussion than the Shield Tag. Which, again, I've tried to facilitate.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms, please feel free to exercise your right to reply but if we can't have a productive and courteous discussion then I'm just going to stop responding to you -- I'm here to help nosleeves (and people I respect like Wizard) enjoy the game, not to spat with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-06-2019, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T01:48:40-07:00","id":1339785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339732#post1339732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's a good baseline to allow players to fix shields however they want.<br /> <br /> For instance you could add these tags :<br /> <br /> -<b>Light/Heavy Cover</b> (1-2) : you can use this weapon to take Light / Heavy Cover (moving ends the effect). If this weapon has the Shield Tag, taking cover behind this weapon can be placed in a Flurry.<br /> -<b>Protective</b> (1) : +1 Parry (cannot be added to Medium Weapons)<br /> <br /> -<b>Medium/Heavy Weight</b> (1-2) : -1 / -2 mobility penalty<br /> -<b>Defensive</b> (-2) : -2 Damage (the rework removes the -2 penalty on shields, this tag brings it back)<br /> -<b>Obstructing</b> (-1) : -1 to vision based Awareness<br /> <br /> <br /> And then you can have these shields :<br /> <br /> <b>Large Shield</b> (Medium) - Melee, Bashing, Shield, Worn, Smashing, Light Cover, Medium Weight, Defensive<br /> <br /> <b>Tower Shield</b> (Heavy) - Melee, Bashing, Shield, Worn, Smashing, Heavy Cover, Protective, Heavy Weight, Defensive, Obstructing</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably set Defensive at -1 (or leave it at -2 but require the Shield tag be bought as well), but otherwise all those ideas are fantastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T04:19:43-07:00","id":1339797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339784#post1339784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to refer you <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339614#post1339614\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, epic fail, that's exactly the post I was talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not trying to represent what other people are saying. </div> </div> </div>And yet, you have done exactly that. &quot;Well, Heavy Arms at least thinks shields are great weapons for controlling the flow of battle.&quot; is a quote from that post. Also earlier on this page: &quot;You think the Shield Tag is a problem because it reduces the amount of Damage shields do and you don't value the benefits of the Tag. (,,,) Because you hold this point of view, you'd like to see shields buffed.&quot; So whatever you're trying to do, it doesn't match your stated intention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm making my point that Shields (the weapon) are more than the Shield Tag. </div> </div> </div>The point is largely meaningless to the discussion. Everything else a shield does besides the Shield Tag is accessible through other options. What can you do with a shield you can't do with a mace besides that doesn't take advantage of the Shield Tag exactly? Because if the answer is &quot;nothing&quot; then what's the point of the point you're trying to make?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm suggesting using the existing system to fix your perceived problem rather than venture into homebrew </div> </div> </div>Anything to fix the problem is homebrew. You have literally argued that adding the Shield Tag to non-medium weapons is homebrew. All the suggestions you've offered are homebrew.<br /> <br /> I'm not advocating writing an entirely new system just to fix shields (I do, however, advocate for an entirely new system to address what I perceive as failures in the weapon and armor system in general; but different groups I play with have different tolerances for how extensive to get with house rules). I'm perfectly comfortable reusing other parts of the system rather than reinventing the wheel, as I already posted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I have an Axe in one hand, the marginal benefits of a shield in the other, in that it allows me to Flurry Full Defence, is more useful than holding a Chopping Sword with redundant Tags. </div> </div> </div>But not more useful than just dual wielding axes, since you'd get the Clash bonus, or you can throw one and still have your preferred weapon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...axiomatic... </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you know what this word means any more, especially considering how hypocritically you're using it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Exalted, since 1st Ed, as in real life some weapons are better than others. </div> </div> </div>And Exalted 3e was sold from it's initial pitch as ditching this and moving to make weapons and armor more balanced to allow weapon and armor selection to be more aesthetic and less optimization focused. I wanted that, and the final product did not deliver on that.<br /> <br /> Even if the goal was to have a range of value to weapons, the RAW in 3e is slapdash and lacking in any noticeable logic or design consideration; largely because they kept things that were originally meant to accomplish the opposite (like no more exceptional weapons, and reducing all weapons to three stat blocks).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're arguing weapons should be unbalanced but shields should be better, then I don't get why. </div> </div> </div>You're still not engaging with the idea of &quot;better in execution,&quot; doesn't have to mean, &quot;buffing them mechanically.&quot; If I'm going to be playing with a group that's comfortable is relatively small house rules (such as adding a Tag, or changing a Tag's function), I'm still designing in the RAW created unbalanced state of things.<br /> <br /> I do not understand what's hard to grasp around the idea of, &quot;I think the execution is bad, so I prefer to use a different way to get to a similar place mechanically,&quot; that you have to consistently misrepresent this as &quot;should be better.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I cannot read this any other way than &quot;I don't care about the published rules of the game&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Try this, &quot;I'm tired of you making arguments that come down to 'the RAW are automatically right/good/etc.' as counterarguments to perceived flaws in the system.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for the mini-link burst? No. You want social credit for stating possible house rules as counting for engaging in discussion. That's not actually being willing to discuss them. When it comes to actually discussing them, you state you don't want to do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When does including Full Defence in your Flurry not have a defensive benefit? </div> </div> </div>When the net bonus from Full Defense + Action = 0. It is, perhaps, an overly semantic point, but it remains an issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Rush action is available inherently and it reduces your Defence. Shields let you Rush (and perform numerous other actions) without lowering your defence. </div> </div> </div>The Rush action doesn't not cost Defense to use, shields don't let you Rush without lowering your Defense. Shields let you boost your Defense by 1 when performing a Rush, at significant cost (-3 to the Rush attempt, -1i).<br /> <br /> It's not about doing something else to reduce the benefit of Full Defence. It's about using a shield to ameliorate defensive penalties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No? Which statement? </div> </div> </div>Your previous statements about not wanting to debate certain topics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you think the issue with shields is not their worth relative to other weapons, then I'm willing to debate this with you. </div> </div> </div>OK... what's your counter-argument to all my stated issues with shields then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With Tags and narrative description. </div> </div> </div>So... everything from a 12 in diameter buckler to a two-man mantlet are all medium weapons because they're classified as shields? It this just to maintain the +1 Parry for medium weapons, or actually thinking all shields should be abstracted as medium despite their ranges in size?<br /> <br /> What Tag represents the difference between a shield that can cover most of your body if you hunker down, but you'll still have some exposed parts, vs. a shield big enough you can hide completely behind it if necessary?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd straight up use the normal Shield stats and model other benefits/penalities with Stunts, Strategems and Command actions. </div> </div> </div>How do any of these represent the differences between a round shield and a scutum? The benefit of Stunts and Command actions aren't going to change. Strategems (unless you're homebrewing new ones) aren't based on your BG's weapon load out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And again, I'd highlight that the rules exist to showcase exceptional heroes, not rank and file. That the system is an abstraction, not a simulation. And that battlegroups are almost certainly Quick Characters and their stats should thus be synthesized to fit the story rather than strictly derived like a PC's. </div> </div> </div>And... exceptional heroes include generals and other military leaders (you know, people that would take lots of dots in War), who might showcase how awesome they are as they turn a bunch of displaced farmers with rudimentary farming tools, into an elite fighting force; including access to high end military weapons and armor. QC abstractions don't include not having access to Tags and such; they use shields like anyone else uses shields.<br /> <br /> If my exceptional hero has trained up a bunch of soldiers pretty well, but they're stuck with light armor and spears by circumstance, and then my PC succeeds in raiding a Legion supply wagon so they have access to lots of new weapons, my QC NPC BG gets new derived actions based on their new equipment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can't Flurry Take Cover with Rush or Disengage. </div> </div> </div>Why not? None of these actions disallow it, and there's no general rule against Flurrying movement actions. If I want to Flurrying Rushing one opponent while Disengaging from a different opponent... that's completely legal (not always smart if the person my PC is chasing figures out to flee towards the characters my PC is trying to get away from).<br /> <br /> Flurrying Take Cover with Rush is kinda pointless if your opponent wants to not deal with Cover, since they can just draw you away from it.<br /> <br /> Flurrying Take Cover and Disengage works just fine. If my PC wants to get out of close combat with a Disengage, and get behind a large stone wall, to avoid ranged attacks from that group... as long as the Cover is there to use, the mechanics support it. And once my PC is behind the wall, I don't need to keep flurrying if I want to continue to try to get away as long as I keep the wall between hostiles and my character.<br /> <br /> If you want a different example?<br /> <br /> Trained combat mounts give me an additional +1 Defense and a bonus to Rush/Disengage which I don't need to Flurry to get. Yes Mounted is defeated by Reach, but Full Defense is defeated by Flexible. So I can get that +1 Defense without dealing with Flurries at all. Not that mounts aren't their own complications, but it's another way to get defensive boosts without shields.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nor is it an objective truth. </div> </div> </div>Good thing I phrased it like it was an opinion or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Read the first post I made in this thread. Then come back and apologise to me. </div> </div> </div>I see nothing to apologize for. Your first post axiomatically treats the bonuses of shields as &quot;powerful,&quot; by just stating they exist, without any actual engagement with the specifics of what they do in application.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you call &quot;projection happy nonsense&quot; is civility. </div> </div> </div>Calling people's positions axiomatic as some magical word to disguise simply dismissing points because you don't agree with the conclusion isn't civil.<br /> <br /> You seem to be one of those people that confuses nice and polite language with civility. Saying things in a &quot;nice&quot; or &quot;polite&quot; or even &quot;academic,&quot; wording doesn't make it civil or not. Civility is in what you use those words to say. There was no civility in the part of your post that<br /> <br /> You've frankly exhausted mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don't want to engage with my argument then don't. </div> </div> </div>When I tried to engage with your arguments, you stated a lack of desire to debate them, and turned the debate back on the argument against shields. It's hard to engage with someone that wants their position to be excluded from the discussion beyond being accepted as sound without examination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's bad faith. </div> </div> </div>Not, it's a critique of your posts. Specifically:<br /> <br /> &quot;Does that change the balance on whether shields are a good thing?&quot;<br /> &quot;If you would, then go back and reread my post.<br /> If you wouldn't, then there's your homebrew solution -- enjoy it. &quot;<br /> <br /> You offer a &quot;suggestion,&quot; but the question is not, &quot;does this address your concerns about shields?&quot; as would befit a desire to honestly engage with ideas on fixing the perceived problems with them. These are leading questions that communicate a desire to use the example ideas as rhetorical devices in the debate rather than as honest suggestions of ways to use the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why is it not a good idea? </div> </div> </div>Do you seriously want to get into the weeds on why a weapon with a flat +2 parry bonus is a bad idea?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Making shields too good makes the decision less interesting and wonks the math behind the abstraction. So, check your premises. </div> </div> </div>What do I need to check? We agree that making shields to good is bad for the same reasons no less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a +1 Parry on Medium weapons is bad for the game, you need to do more than fix the Shield Tag to fix Shields. </div> </div> </div>I know, I've said as much, repeatedly. Have you considered that maybe... you're not reading me all that closely?<br /> <br /> Of course, I said the +1 Parry on medium weapons is questionable for the game, because many of the issues come from interactions with a few moving parts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which, again, I've tried to facilitate. </div> </div> </div>It would be really nice if you stopped conflating just asserting/stating something with things like having discussions about it, or facilitating discussions about it.<br /> <br /> Of course the whole attempt to make things about &quot;balance&quot; is just another bit of nuisance rather than helpful or civil discourse. There are plenty of complaints about how shields work that aren't based on any sense of overall balance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heavy Arms, please feel free to exercise your right to reply but if we can't have a productive and courteous discussion then I'm just going to stop responding to you -- I'm here to help nosleeves (and people I respect like Wizard) enjoy the game, not to spat with you. </div> </div> </div>And... another great example of how &quot;nice words&quot; is vastly different from civility.<br /> <br /> If you want a more productive and courteous discussion, spare me condescending bullshit like this attempt to puff yourself up as the &quot;good guy.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T06:14:53-07:00","id":1339815,"title":"","content":"Let's dial it back a bit, yeah guys? Getting a bit overheated here. I think we're getting a bit stuck on specific statements that aren't all that important.<br /> <br /> Why don't we dial back to &quot;how would you write shields&quot; rather than &quot;why you are wrong about that thing you just said.&quot; Like Epitome has done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T06:24:14-07:00","id":1339818,"title":"","content":"Anything break if you...drop Medium Weapons +1 parry and make that unique to shields?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T06:32:29-07:00","id":1339820,"title":"","content":"So here's my opinion on the shields in 3e.<br /> <br /> I despise their existance because they don't do what a shield does.<br /> <br /> Give a character superior defense to anyone without a shield.<br /> <br /> bonuses when rushing and stuff sure sure.<br /> <br /> BUUUUUUT they don't affect the ACTUAL fighting part of the fight.<br /> <br /> It's essentially a case of two boxers taking cars to a fight and one of them have bulletproof glass.<br /> That's what a shield feels like in 3e.<br /> AND THAT'S BAD!<br /> <br /> In a melee fight, the guy with the shield is pretty much always going to beat those without one.<br /> Not to mention that you will be the one controlling the fight if you have a shield and the opponent doesn't.<br /> <br /> You can hide what angle your strike comes from with the shield.<br /> You can deny the enemy the ability to strike properly by ramming her up against the wall with your shield.<br /> You can use it to strike the enemy so there's that.<br /> With a tower shield, you can take most infantry charges far better than those without one since you can brace and have the impact distributed far more than those without one.<br /> If the enemy tries to kick you in the shin and you have a tower shield you can just slam that sucker down and break their foot, pretty much guaranteeing you victory (an opponent that can't walk usually can't win).<br /> And it can be used to PROTECT YOU FROM ATTACKS AT ALL RANGES!<br /> <br /> The current iteration of shields keeps the damn stupid concept that you can't fight behind a shield and that you need to open up to strike.<br /> <br /> Sure, a shield won't be as deadly as most dedicated weapons cutting knife a pretty big exception as it will mostly just give you shallow cuts that might end up bleeding you out but at the same time you will probably have brought down your shield on their face enough times to turn them into mush.<br /> <br /> And those are things you can do as just a normal person.<br /> <br /> As one of the chosen you could be running around with strength 5 shields and just use their massive weight to pretty much just pancake the enemy under them.<br /> Heck, you can just drop it on their feet then flip it down on them.<br /> What are they going to do if they can't attempt strength 5 feats of strength?<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's my rant.<br /> <br /> Now on to what could be used.<br /> <br /> Flat defense boost but to make things &quot;balanced&quot; you can actually slap that -2 damage on all of your attacks but at the same time you gain that bonus to defense and possibly no penalty from flurries and/or depending on test results, the ability to perform withering attacks in a full defense flurry.<br /> If that seems OP then just make it directional.<br /> If the guy has a massive shield that you can't get through then you try to get at him from the sides or from behind.<br /> Use stunts, be creative USE YOUR DAMN IMAGINATION!<br /> <br /> But that's just my thoughts and simple ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T06:42:03-07:00","id":1339821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339818#post1339818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything break if you...drop Medium Weapons +1 parry and make that unique to shields?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically no, but balance-wise it might create a situation where everyone with a free offhand is incentivized to carry a shield for the +1 Parry.<br /> <br /> I know this problem technically already exists with Medium weapons as a whole, but taking the +1 Parry and putting it only on shields might compound the issue and make the average Circle always carry 2-3 Shields for gameplay reasons rather than because it fits the characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T06:45:16-07:00","id":1339824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339821#post1339821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mechanically no, but balance-wise it might create a situation where everyone with a free offhand is incentivized to carry a shield for the +1 Parry.<br /> <br /> I know this problem technically already exists with Medium weapons as a whole, but taking the +1 Parry and putting it only on shields might compound the issue and make the average Circle always carry 2-3 Shields for gameplay reasons rather than because it fits the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>how about a initiative costing damage boost in the form of the character using both hands to strike as compensation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T06:51:15-07:00","id":1339828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339824#post1339824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how about a initiative costing damage boost in the form of the character using both hands to strike as compensation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you create an incentive to use only 1 one-handed weapon then things could work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T09:03:25-07:00","id":1339856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339818#post1339818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything break if you...drop Medium Weapons +1 parry and make that unique to shields?</div> </div> </div> </div>You vastly incentivise shields, weaken paired Medium weapons and make Clashes more desirable. Personally, I don't like it but it's a lot less derailing than giving Shields +2 Parry.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339820#post1339820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flat defense boost but to make things &quot;balanced&quot; you can actually slap that -2 damage on all of your attacks but at the same time you gain that bonus to defense and possibly no penalty from flurries and/or depending on test results, the ability to perform withering attacks in a full defense flurry.<br /> If that seems OP then just make it directional.<br /> If the guy has a massive shield that you can't get through then you try to get at him from the sides or from behind.<br /> Use stunts, be creative USE YOUR DAMN IMAGINATION!</div> </div> </div> </div>I would worry about taking a permanent damage debuff for an advantage my foes can ignore with a Stunt. I'd suggest going with one or the other drawback.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339828#post1339828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, if you create an incentive to use only 1 one-handed weapon then things could work out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd suggest something like Indivisible's idea to let people two-hand a single one handed weapon for the Clash bonus. Then you sword and board for static parry and dual wield or freehand duel to Clash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T09:16:48-07:00","id":1339860,"title":"","content":"One thing that is glaring to me is how they are not all that good for BGs, which are pretty much the scenarios where shields dominate the most. So we might as well simply tack that on to BGs:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Shield tag, for battlegroups, allows Full Defense flurries without i costs (for long term usability). BGs with standard drill or better can also flurry in attacks. Elite Drill also removes the flurry defense penalty. </div> </div> </div>BGs' inflated attack pools compensate for the attack penalty, while giving a better baseline defense proportional to the training. Opposing uncommanded BGs will drag on, but since games revolving around BGs are either those with or against the players, I feel the Exalted will still make short work of them if built for it. The former can be relegated to the background.<br /> <br /> I am content with most of the minutia in the advantages of shields being basically stunt fodder, and leave to the Exalted the deeds that go beyond, exploiting offensive and defensive advantages that would normally be irreconcilable or too difficult to work with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#0095C6\">Soaring on the wings of Sol and Mars</span></b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Dipping Swallow Defense, Excellent Strike<br /> <br /> Shields are among the most distinctive weapons in the battlefield, and the Exalt has learned to blend flexible defense and overbearing control above and beyond his peers on the battlefield.<br /> Pick 3 benefits to use armed with a shield. Others can be bought for 2xp each.<br /> <br /> <b>Flashing Bulwark's edge:</b> The shield loses its -2 damage penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Walls light as feathers:</b> Full Defenses with the shield no longer cost 1i, and can be done in crash.<br /> <br /> <b>Infinitely Adaptable Tactics:</b> Full Defenses can be flurried without a defense penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Overbearing Momentum:</b> Clashes with the shield benefit from the +2 bonus of a 2-handed weapon.<br /> <br /> <b>Daggers-through-walls Style:</b> For 2m, you may flurry Full Defense with any action that can normally be placed in a flurry.<br /> <br /> <b>Advancing Enceinte:</b> Essence reinforces the shield and resonates back onto the Solar, adding [Essence] to her armored soak against attacks that hit through her parry. If the solar is unarmored the bonus increases by 3. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T09:22:39-07:00","id":1339861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339856#post1339856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest something like Indivisible's idea to let people two-hand a single one handed weapon for the Clash bonus. Then you sword and board for static parry and dual wield or freehand duel to Clash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd try to go with something else, possibly a bonus to the initiative roll?<br /> Just to give it a difference from the dual wield just to give the rather stale weapon choices a bit more difference between the different wielding styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T12:51:00-07:00","id":1339886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339818#post1339818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything break if you...drop Medium Weapons +1 parry and make that unique to shields?</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's all you change?<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> The basic problem as it stands here, is that mathwise before getting into Tags, medium weapons are effectively the best weapons because of that +1 Parry (esp. mundane weapons). So stripping the +1 Parry alone just makes most medium weapons inferior to their light counterparts, and heavy weapons continue to lag behind (baring shield + lance mounted).<br /> <br /> So, on top of what everyone's already said about incentives to off-hand a shield just for the Parry boost (which to me isn't exactly bad, but it maintains the problem of shields being seen as passive items instead of active weapons), you're devaluing a whole class of weapon to make it happen.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons a bunch of people are intrigued by Storypath's approach of not even having weapon stat lines at all, and do everything with Tags instead: no need to worry about how light vs. medium vs. heavy compare to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T14:21:36-07:00","id":1339916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339684#post1339684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your example doesn't explain anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is par for the course, because examples don't explain, they demonstrate. What the Martial Artist Merit very clearly demonstrates is that Exalted 3rd's design was, as you actually noticed, &quot;oriented around Exalts&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339684#post1339684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't validily claim the rules aren't built for something that's built into the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure I can, because the game itself says so.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted rulebook, boxed text, p.125</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you\u2019re new to Storytelling, you might want to get your feet wet by running a game where everyone plays a mortal. Alternately, you might want to run a chronicle where your players\u2019 characters start off mortal and Exalt during play.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the explicitly-stated purposes of the mortal characters rules, given in the first paragraph of the box on those rules, are that they are for games where: A) you're getting comfortable with the system, or B) as the introductory part of a game playing Exalts.<br /> <br /> If you're using the Exalted rules to play a full-scale mortals game, you're using them for something they weren't intended to support. When you're using rules for a purpose other than the ones explicitly given as the intended uses, it's only to be expected that you'll run into difficulties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T15:44:47-07:00","id":1339945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339916#post1339916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the Martial Artist Merit very clearly demonstrates is that Exalted 3rd's design was, as you actually noticed, &quot;oriented around Exalts&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>One Merit hardly demonstrates this. The whole Supernatural Merit list isn't &quot;oriented&quot; around Exalts, and one of them is for giving non-Exalts a power all Exalts get automatically, and another all Exalted Sorcerers get automatically on getting TCS.<br /> <br /> The game is written with the expectation that default play is to play the Exalted, that doesn't mean there is no intention in the text to support playing mortals as a secondary way to use the game... in fact...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, the explicitly-stated purposes of the mortal characters rules... </div> </div> </div>The sheer existence of this is a demonstration against your point. Exalted, as directly stated by the core book, is meant to support playing mortals as part of the game.<br /> <br /> You're arguing the rules don't support playing mortals... while citing a passage telling you that the rules support playing mortals. Why you're playing mortals and for how long doesn't really impact this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're using the Exalted rules to play a full-scale mortals game, you're using them for something they weren't intended to support. </div> </div> </div>According to the text, as you cited, playing a full-scale mortals game is an intended use of the game that the rules are intended to support. The intention is to do this as a stepping stone/teaching method before playing Exalted focused games, but that doesn't diminish the idea that the rules are, in fact, intended to run a mortals game with support from the text.<br /> <br /> If playing a mortals game to learn the general systems before getting into all the additional Exalt specific systems, is a supported form of play (which again, the passage you just cited says it is), then what's the difference between playing mortals for learning the game, and playing mortals for the sake of playing mortals, in terms of what the rules support?<br /> <br /> The only issue I've ever seen that's specific to this, is that mortals run out of XP to spend things on as they don't have access to as many options as Exalts do (though they don't get Solar/etc. XP either).<br /> <br /> Even the MA Merit issue isn't really a factor of playing mortals to learn vs. playing to play mortals. The problem with requiring the Merit for mortals to pick up MA Ability dots impacts learning the systems too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you're using rules for a purpose other than the ones explicitly given as the intended uses, it's only to be expected that you'll run into difficulties. </div> </div> </div>Actually, the problem is when you're using the rules for a purpose that game gives as intended uses.<br /> <br /> 1) The thread of quotes that got us here was not even about playing mortals or not, but about how abstracted shield should be. The connection between shields and mortals is that they're things in the book that are given rules that we're supposed to use to play. Saying, &quot;ignore this stuff about shields, the system is abstract and ignore things like helmets,&quot; doesn't work when the book as detail rules for shields. Likewise, &quot;Exalted isn't intended to support playing mortals,&quot; doesn't work when the book directly tells you it supports playing mortals to learn the general rules of the game, or to play pre-Exalted characters; those both require supporting mortal play.<br /> <br /> 2) The complaints about shields don't rely on them not working right for mortals, but working fine for Exalts. All of my issues with shields don't change if the character wielding them is an Exalt without specific Charms. The complaint that shields are meaningless in a one-on-one duel doesn't change if the characters are Exalts or not. Etc. The importance of shields and mortals is in BGs; and is only mortal focused because most BGs are made up of mortals. Whether a heroic mortal commanding a Legion, or an Abyssal warlord commanding an army of undead, shields not really doing anything for BGs is the complaint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T18:59:04-07:00","id":1339975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339174-shield-mechanics?p=1339916#post1339916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're using the Exalted rules to play a full-scale mortals game, you're using them for something they weren't intended to support. When you're using rules for a purpose other than the ones explicitly given as the intended uses, it's only to be expected that you'll run into difficulties.</div> </div> </div> </div>-stops reading-<br /> <br /> -looks at the several different and complete mortal campaigns he has written and ran in the last few years, involving small-scale and mass-combat, politics, nation and dynasty-building, trade and more, <i><b><u>all using the mechanics for such presenting in the Core Book 99.99% as written</u></b></i>-<br /> <br /> -looks at above quote-<br /> <br /> - eyebrow takes off into stratosphere-<br /> <br /> You are so incorrect, it is actually impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T00:45:30-07:00","id":1340002,"title":"","content":"*hopes to hear more ideas*<br /> I have to admit I'm at a loss for what to do to make shields more appealing that is easy to implement.<br /> Right now it looks like there are no easy changes to make that don't potentially break something else.<br /> <br /> My players have now played from ess1 to ess5 in 3e and no one has ever looked twice at a shield. It's not even the damage penalty that is off-putting for them, it is that flurrying rush with full defence is not seen as a benefit for them. In the years playing there have been maybe two or three rush attempts ever. Cover on the other hand does tend to be used.<br /> I don't think this particular tag is uniquely disliked though. The higher the defence and init cost the less likely (loath to use really) players are to use the tag. The most popular weapons have been those with balanced, grappling, and disarming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T02:04:16-07:00","id":1340005,"title":"","content":"Implementing a Cover Tag isn't terribly hard.<br /> <br /> I've had decent success with two options, depending a bit on the test groups tolerances for options:<br /> <br /> 1) Passive light cover, subject to flanking*<br /> <br /> 2) Passive cover (none/light/heavy) and mobility penalty (0, -1, -2) based on weapon type, increase the level of cover by one with the Take Cover action (subject to normal Flurry rules), still subject to flanking*<br /> <br /> * - Flanking is a subjective concept relating to how Cover works, basically, you have to declare a direction or a target you're aiming the shield at, anything that's reasonably to the side of the shield ignores it's Cover just like any other form of Cover.<br /> <br /> #1 is nice because it's straightforward and easy.<br /> <br /> #2 is better for people looking for more variety, since it makes a light buckler feel significantly different from a heavy scutum without wildly different rules. The mobility penalty and ability to get flanked keeps the Defense bonus in check so they can't just steam roll ranged units, and close range you have to commit as the mobility penalty makes it hard to run while the Defense bonus is a bit of a wash.<br /> <br /> Getting a Flurry Full Defense Tag to work in a more appealing fashion has proven a bit more difficult. When I've tried, coupling it with the Clash bonus seems to be a bigger appeal, but it does mean people take it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}